<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="JAS" style="id" />
  <para style="h">YAKOBO</para>
  <para style="toc1">Waraga ma Yakobo Ocoyo</para>
  <para style="toc2">Yakobo</para>
  <para style="toc3">Yak</para>
  <para style="mt2">Waraga ma</para>
  <para style="mt1">YAKOBO</para>
  <para style="mt2">Ocoyo</para>
  <para style="imt">Lanyut wilok madito ma i buk man</para>
  <para style="ip">Waraga man ma oa ki bot Yakobo ni opong ki pwony mapatpat ma kicoyo bot “Jo pa Lubanga ducu ma guket ata i lobo ducu”. Lacoc man tiyo ki labol mapatpat me miyo pwony ikit yo ma lakricitayo myero okwo kwede. En nyutu kit ma lakricitayo myero onen lok mamako lonyo, can, atematema, berkit, niye wa ki tic malube ki niye bene. Kit me tic ki leb, lok ma mako ryeko, daa, awaka ki mwolo, ngolo kop ikom dano, bute, diyo cwiny ki lega.</para>
  <para style="ip">Waraga man keto kili ikom lok ma mako niye ki tic ma kitiyo malube ki niye.</para>
  <para style="iot">Lacim wilok madito ma i buk man</para>
  <para style="io1">Lanyut <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 1:1">1:1</ref></char></para>
  <para style="io1">Niye ki Ryeko <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 1:2-8">1:2-8</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Can ki Lonyo <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 1:9-11">1:9-11</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Atematema ki Abita <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 1:12-18">1:12-18</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Winyo lok ki ketone i tic <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 1:19-27">1:19-27</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Apokapoka ma tere peke <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 2:1-13">2:1-13</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Niye ki tice <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 2:14-26">2:14-26</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Lakricitayo ki lebe <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 3:1-18">3:1-18</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Lakricitayo ki lobo <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 4:1-5:6">4:1—5:6</ref> </char></para>
  <para style="io1">Pwony mapatpat <char style="ior"><ref loc="JAS 5:7-20">5:7-20</ref> </char></para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JAS 1" />
  <para style="s1">Mot</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 1:1" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">1:1: </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 13:55">Mat 13:55</ref>; <ref loc="MRK 6:3">Mar 6:3</ref>; <ref loc="ACT 15:13">Tic 15:13</ref>; <ref loc="GAL 1:19">Gal 1:19</ref></char>
    </note> Waraga man oa ki bot an Yakobo ma latic pa Lubanga ki pa Rwotwa Yecu Kricito.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="JAS 1:1">Bot kaka apar wiye aryo ma guket woko ata ikin piny: Amotowu ba.<verse eid="JAS 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Niye ki Ryeko</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 1:2" />Utmegina, wubed ki yomcwiny madwong ka kitemowu i yo mapatpat, <verse eid="JAS 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 1:3" />pien wungeyo ni temo niyewu miyo wudiyo cwinywu. <verse eid="JAS 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 1:4" />Wek diyo cwiny ocob tice kakare, wek wubed jo muteggi, ma roc mo pe ikomwu, dok wubed ma gin mo bene pe orem botwu.<verse eid="JAS 1:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 1:5" />Kace ngat mo tye ikinwu ma ryekone nok, myero en oleg Lubanga ma miyo bot jo ducu ki yomcwiny, kun pe twono ngat mo; ci bimiye. <verse eid="JAS 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 1:6" />Ento myero en oleg ki niye, labongo akalakala mo; pien ngat ma bedo ki akalakala rom ki pii me nam ma twage, ma yamo coro tagge atata. <verse eid="JAS 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 1:7" />Kit dano macalo meno myero pe otam ni ebinongo gin mo ki bot Rwot, <verse eid="JAS 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 1:8" />pien en bedo ma tame aryo, ma pe cung matek ikit yo me kwo ne ducu.<verse eid="JAS 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Can ki lonyo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 1:9" />Lacan myero owake ka Lubanga omedo rwome malo, <verse eid="JAS 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 1:10" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">1:10: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="ISA 40:6">Ica 40:6</ref>,<ref loc="ISA 40:7">7</ref></char></note> lalonyo bene kitmeno myero owake ka Lubanga odwoko rwome piny; pien lalonyo birwenyo woko calo tur lum. <verse eid="JAS 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 1:11" />Pien ceng tuc ki lyetone matek, ci nero lum, ture o, bere bene rwenyo woko. Lalonyo bene birwenyo woko ata kitmeno i dye tice me kare ducu.<verse eid="JAS 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Temo cwiny ki bita</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 1:12" />Ngat ma kitemo cwinye tye ki gum ce ocung matek; pien ka dong kiteme, ce en oloyo, ci binongo mot me lalukana me kwo ma Rwot ociko me miyo bot jo ma maro en. <verse eid="JAS 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 1:13" />Ka kibito ngat mo, en pe myero owaci, “Lubanga aye ma bita,” pien Lubanga pe bite ki gin marac, en bene pe bito ngat mo. <verse eid="JAS 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 1:14" />Dano acel acel gire mitine kene aye ma bite, ywaye, kun omo cwinye. <verse eid="JAS 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 1:15" />Miti ka oyac ci nywalo bal. Bal ka dong odongo muteggi nywalo to.<verse eid="JAS 1:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 1:16" />Utmegina ma amaro, pe wuwek kibwolwu. <verse eid="JAS 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 1:17" />Pien kit gin mo ducu maber, ki mot ducu mabeco tutwal ma kimiyowa, a ki malo, a ki bot Lubanga Won bino piny, ma en aye won dero ducu ma i polo, ma pe tye ki alokaloka mo, dok tipu mo ma nyutu lokene bene pe. <verse eid="JAS 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 1:18" />Pi mitine gire kene, en onywalowa ki loke me ada, wek wabed calo cam ma i poto mukwongo cek ki ikin ginacweya ducu.<verse eid="JAS 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Winyo lok ki ketone i tic</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 1:19" />Utmegina ma amaro, wunge lok man. Dano acel acel myero owiny lok oyotoyot, ento pe myero orune me gamone, dok bene pe omyero owek kiniga omake oyot. <verse eid="JAS 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 1:20" />Pien kiniga pa dano pe cobo tic ma atir inyim Lubanga. <verse eid="JAS 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 1:21" />Wubol gin ducu me lewic woko cen ki tim maracu madong onya botwu, wek wugam lok pa Lubanga ma opito i iwu ki mwolo, pien twero laro tipuwu. <verse eid="JAS 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 1:22" />Ento wubed jo ma keto gin ma giloko i tic, pe wubed jo ma winyo awinya keken kun wubwole kenwu. <verse eid="JAS 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 1:23" />Pien kace dano mo obedo lawiny lok keken ma pe tiyo, ci bedo calo ngat ma ngiyo wange i kiyo. <verse eid="JAS 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 1:24" />Ento ka dong otyeko ngiine kekene, cito woko, ci wiye wil woko oyotoyot i calle ma en obedo kanenone tutwali. <verse eid="JAS 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 1:25" />Ento ngat maneno cik maber makelo kuc, ka orii iye, ma pe bedo calo ngat ma winyo ka dok wiye wil woko, ento ngat ma keto lok ma en owinyo i tic, kibimiye gum i gin ma en otiyo ducu.<verse eid="JAS 1:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 1:26" />Kace dano mo otamo ni en ladini kun pe juku lebe, nongo bwole abwola kene ki i cwinye, dininenu konye peke. <verse eid="JAS 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JAS 1:27" />Dini me ada maleng, ma cilo pe iye inyim Lubanga Wonwa en ene: konyo lutino kic ki mon ma coggi oto ikom can ma gitye kwede, ki gwoke ken ikom bal me lobo.<verse eid="JAS 1:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JAS 2" />
  <para style="s1">Gwoke ikom tim me apokapoka</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 2:1" />Utmegina, kit macalo dong wuye Rwotwa Yecu Kricito kwedeni, ma en Rwot me deyo, pe dok wukel apokapoka mo ikin dano. <verse eid="JAS 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 2:2" />Pien kace won agit jabu oruku bongi mabeco obino kwede i cokewu, ki lacan bene oruku bongi mugenyogeny, <verse eid="JAS 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 2:3" />ce wukwongo tamo pi dano ma oruku bongi mabeconi, kun wuwaco ni, “Bed kany, ladit,” ento bot lacan wuwace ni, “Cung kuca,” nyo ni, “Bed piny katyena kany.” <verse eid="JAS 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 2:4" />Meno nongo pe dong wukelo apokapoka woko ikinwu kekenwu, kun wudoko bene lungolkop ma tamwu ogom woko?<verse eid="JAS 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 2:5" />Wuwiny ba, utmegina ma amaro, pe Lubanga aye ma oyero jo ma lucan iwi lobo wek gubed lulonyo i niye, dok me miyogi ker mayam ociko ni ebimiyo bot jo ma mare? <verse eid="JAS 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 2:6" />Ento wun wuketo lewic ikom lucan. Pe lulonyo aye ma buruwu? Pe gin aye ma ywayowu kun giterowu tektek inyim lungolkop? <verse eid="JAS 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 2:7" />Pe gin aye luyet nying maber ma kilwongowu kwedeni?<verse eid="JAS 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 2:8" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">2:8: </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="LEV 19:18">Lev 19:18</ref>
      </char>
    </note> Kace wumako cik me ker pa Lubanga kit mayam kicoyo kwede i ginacoya ni, “Mar lawoti macalo imare keni,” nongo wutimo ber; <verse eid="JAS 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 2:9" />ento kace wupoko kin dano, nongo wutimo rac, nongo Cik ngolo kop ikomwu ni wun lubalo. <verse eid="JAS 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 2:10" />Pien ngat ma gwoko cik ducu, kace opoto i cik acel keken, nongo oturu cik ducu. <verse eid="JAS 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 2:11" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2:11: a </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="EXO 20:14">Nia 20:14</ref>; <ref loc="DEU 5:18">Nwo 5:18</ref>; </char><char style="xo" closed="false">b </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="EXO 20:13">Nia 20:13</ref>; <ref loc="DEU 5:17">Nwo 5:17</ref></char></note> Pien ngat ma owaco ni, “Pe i tim abor,” owaco bene ni, “Pe ineki.” Ka inen ce pe itimo abor ento ineko dano, nongo dong ituru Cik. <verse eid="JAS 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 2:12" />Lok ma wuloko, ki gin ma wutiyo, myero obed macalo pa jo ma kibingolo kop ikomgi ite Cik makelo kuc. <verse eid="JAS 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 2:13" />Pien pe kibitimo kica bot ngat mayam pe otimo kica; ento ka in ibedo ngat ma timo kica, ci Lubanga bitimo kica ka en ngolo kop ikomi.<verse eid="JAS 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Niye ma pe ki tic</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 2:14" />Konyo gin ango, utmegina, ka ngat mo waco ni etye ki niye kun pe keto i tic? Ci niye meno twero lare? <verse eid="JAS 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 2:15" />Kace omeru nyo lameru peke ki bongo, kun cam me nino ducu bene remo, <verse eid="JAS 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 2:16" />ci ngat mo ikinwu waco botgi ni, “Wucit ki kuc, komwu obed mormor, wubed ma wuyeng,” kun pe wumiyo botgi gin mo mamite pi pito kom, ci meno konyo ango? <verse eid="JAS 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 2:17" />Kitmeno, niye kene ka pe kiketo i tic, nongo dong oto woko. <verse eid="JAS 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 2:18" />Ngat mo biwaco ni, “In itye ki niye, ento an atye ki tic; nyuta niyeni labongo tic mo, ka dong abinyuti niyena ki tica.” <verse eid="JAS 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 2:19" />Iye ni Lubanga tye acel, itimo ber. Kadi cen gu bene giye kitmeno, dok komgi myel. <verse eid="JAS 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 2:20" />In laming, i mito kinyuti ni, niye ma pe ki tic konye pe? <verse eid="JAS 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 2:21" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2:21: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="GEN 22:1-14">Aca 22:1-14</ref></char></note> Kwarowa Abraim yam pe kikwano ni kite atir pi tic, ikare ma en otyero wode Icaka me bedo gitum iwi keno tyer? <verse eid="JAS 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 2:22" />Dong ineno ni niyene yam ocobe ki tic, <verse eid="JAS 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 2:23" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2:23: a </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="GEN 15:6">Aca 15:6</ref>; </char><char style="xo" closed="false">b </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="2CH 20:7">2 Tek 20:7</ref>; <ref loc="ISA 41:8">Ica 41:8</ref></char></note> omiyo lok mayam kicoyo ocobe kakare ni, “Abraim oye Lubanga, omiyo kikwane ni en dano ma kite atir”; dok bene kilwonge ni en larem Lubanga. <verse eid="JAS 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 2:24" />Dong ineno ni dano kikwane ni kite atir pi tice, ento pe pi niye keken. <verse eid="JAS 2:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 2:25" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">2:25: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="JOS 2:1-21">Yoc 2:1-21</ref></char></note> Kitmeno bene, Rakab, dako ma malaya, pe yam kikwane ni kite atir pi tice, ikare mayam en ojolo lukwena ka lacen ocwalogi gucito woko i yo mukene? <verse eid="JAS 2:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 2:26" />Kit macalo kayweyo dong pe ikom, nongo kom dong oto woko, kitmeno bene, niye ka pe kiketo i tic, nongo dong oto woko.<verse eid="JAS 2:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JAS 3" />
  <para style="s1">Gwoko lebi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 3:1" />Utmegina, pe myero jo mapol ikinwu gudok lupwony, pien wungeyo ni wan lupwony kibingolo kop mapek iwiwa makato jo mukene. <verse eid="JAS 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 3:2" />Wan ducu ngat acel acel timo lwak roc mapol, ento kace inen ngat mo pe roco i gin ma en loko, ci danoni nongo dano maber tutwal, twero loyo kome ducu. <verse eid="JAS 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 3:3" />Wan warwako nyonyo i dog aguragura wek guwinywa, ci wawiro komgi ducu dok tung kama wamito. <verse eid="JAS 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 3:4" />Kong wunen mel, ginen dongo mada, dok yamo aye ma kologi, ento ngat ma kwango twero wiro cito kama en mito ki latin pol mo matidi keken. <verse eid="JAS 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 3:5" />Kitmeno, leb obedo dul kom manen tidi mo, ento wake mada i jami madongo. Nen kit ma mac matidi mo keken wango kwede bunga madit!<verse eid="JAS 3:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 3:6" />Leb bene obedo calo mac. Ikin dul komwa leb rom ki lobo ma gin ma en tiyo pe atir, ci balo komwa woko ducu. Leb cwinyo kwowa ki mac ma pe to. <verse eid="JAS 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 3:7" />Dano twero loyo kit lee ducu, wa winyi, twol gu ki ginacweya ducu ma bedo i nam, dok bene guloyogi woko yam con. <verse eid="JAS 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 3:8" />Ento pe tye dano mo matwero loyo leb. Leb aye twon gin mo ma pe juke, opong ki kwir ma neko dano. <verse eid="JAS 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 3:9" />Leb en aye gin ma wapako kwede Rwot Lubanga Wonwa, en leb acelu bene waceno kwede dano ma kicweyogi i cal pa Lubanga kikome. <verse eid="JAS 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 3:10" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">3:10: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="GEN 1:26">Aca 1:26</ref></char></note> Miyo pwoc ki ceno dano a i dog acelu. Utmegina, pe myero obed kitmeno. <verse eid="JAS 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 3:11" />Wang it acel mono twero mol iye pii mamit ki makece? <verse eid="JAS 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 3:12" />Utmegina, oduru mono twero nyak yaa? Nyo olok twero nyak oduru? Kitmeno pii mamit bene pe twero mol kun a ki iwang it ma piine obedo kadokado.<verse eid="JAS 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ryeko ma oa ki malo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 3:13" />Anga ikinwu maryek dok niang jami? En myero onyut tic me ryekone ki mwolo, pi kwo ne maber. <verse eid="JAS 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 3:14" />Ento ka wutye ki nyeko icwinywu, paro piri keni, pe wuwake, pe bene wuwac lok goba ikom lok ada. <verse eid="JAS 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 3:15" />Kit ryeko macalo meno pe oa ki i polo ento obedo me lobo, pe woro Lubanga, ento pa Catan. <verse eid="JAS 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 3:16" />Pien kama nyeko ki paro piri keni tye iye, inongo anyobanyoba ki tim ducu maracu tye iye. <verse eid="JAS 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 3:17" />Ento ryeko ma oa ki malo mukwongo, bedo leng, dok bedo me kuc, me mwolo, gamo tam ducu mabeco, opong ki kica, ki nyako nyig maber, ngat matye kwede pe poko kin dano, pe bedo ngat ma labute. <verse eid="JAS 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 3:18" />Jo makelo kuc gicoyo kodigi i kuc me nyako kit ma atir.<verse eid="JAS 3:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JAS 4" />
  <para style="s1">Mako Larem ki lobo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 4:1" />Gin ango makelo daa, ki gin ango makelo lweny ikinwu? Pe par ma wutye kwede aye tye kalweny i dul komwu? <verse eid="JAS 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 4:2" />Wumito wunong jami, ento pe wunongo, ci wucako neko dano. Dok wuparo jami pa jo mukene, ento pe wunongo, ka dong wuero daa ki lweny. Pe wunongo gin ma wumito, pien pe wulego. <verse eid="JAS 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 4:3" />Wulego ento pe wunongo, pien wulego marac, wulego ni wunong wek wutii kwede me cobo mitiwu keken. <verse eid="JAS 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 4:4" />Wun jo ma pe wugene. Pe wungeyo ni mako larem ki lobo miyo dano doko lakwor pa Lubanga? Pimeno, ngat ma mito mako larem ki lobo loke kene doko lakwor pa Lubanga. <verse eid="JAS 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 4:5" />Nyo wutamo ni, lok mayam kicoyoni obedo lok ma tere pe ni, “En tye ki par madwong tutwal ki nyeko ikom cwiny mayam en oketo ni obed i iwa?” <verse eid="JAS 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 4:6" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4:6: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="PRO 3:34">Car 3:34</ref> </char></note> Ento en mede ki miyo kicane; pimeno, lok mayam kicoyo waco ni, “Lubanga dag jo ma wake, ento miyo kica bot jo mamwol.” <verse eid="JAS 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 4:7" />Pimeno, wumiine kenwu me bedo ite loc pa Lubanga. Wulweny matek ki Catan, ci en biringowu woko. <verse eid="JAS 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 4:8" />Wunyik cok bot Lubanga, ci en bene binyiko cok botwu. Wulwok cingwu woko, wun lubalo, ka dong wulony cwinywu obed maleng, wun jo ma tamwu tye aryo. <verse eid="JAS 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 4:9" />Cwinywu myero owang, wukum, wukok bene. Nyerowu myero oloke odok kumu, ki yomcwiny ma wutye kwede oloke odok can. <verse eid="JAS 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 4:10" />Wumwole kenwu inyim Rwot, ci en bitingowu malo.<verse eid="JAS 4:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ngolo kop ikom dano mukene</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 4:11" />Utmegina, pe wulok lok mo marac kun ngat acel acel loko ikom lawote. Ngat ma loko lok marac ikom lawote, nyo ngolo kop ikom lawote, nongo oloko lok marac ikom cik, nongo dong bene ongolokop ikom cik. Ento ka in ingolo kop ikom cik, in dong pe lacob cik ento idoko langolkop. <verse eid="JAS 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 4:12" />Lamii cik ki langolkop tye acel, en twero larowu ki nekowu. In anga mono ma ingolo kop ikom lawotini?<verse eid="JAS 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Cik ikom wake</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 4:13" />Kong wuwiny loka, wun ma wuwaco ni, “Tin nyo diki wabicito i taun munyo, wabityeko kunu mwaka acel kun wacato wil dok wanongo magoba,” <verse eid="JAS 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 4:14" />kun kono pe wungeyo lok ma bitime diki. Kwowu tye ningning? Wun wubedo calo lupuu manen pi kare manok mo keken, ci lacen ke woko. <verse eid="JAS 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 4:15" />Ma ka loko lok kitmeno, onongo myero wuwac ni, “Ka Rwot oye, wabibedo kwo, wabitimo man nyo maca.” <verse eid="JAS 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 4:16" />Ento wun lunyate, dok wuwake bene. Lakit wake macalo meno ducu rac. <verse eid="JAS 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 4:17" />Ngat ma ngeyo gin ma atir ma myero etim, ce pe otimo, nongo dong otimo bal.<verse eid="JAS 4:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="JAS 5" />
  <para style="s1">Lok ma kiciko ki lulonyo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 5:1" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">5:1: </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 6:19">Mat 6:19</ref>
      </char>
    </note> Wuwiny ba, wun lulonyo, wukoki, dok wudange, pi can ma bipoto ikomwu. <verse eid="JAS 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 5:2" />Lonyowu dong otop woko, kadi ki ginarukawu bene nyenye ocamo woko. <verse eid="JAS 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 5:3" />Jabu ki ryalwu, nyal dong omako woko; nyal kikome aye bibedo caden ikomwu, dok bicamo komwu woko calo mac. Wun dong wutyeko kano lonyo pi kare me agiki. <verse eid="JAS 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 5:4" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5:4: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="DEU 24:14">Nwo 24:14</ref>,<ref loc="DEU 24:15">15</ref></char></note> Nen mucara pa lutic ma gitiyo i potiwu ma wutwonogi woko, tye kakok; koko pa lukac dong owinye bot Rwot me mony. <verse eid="JAS 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 5:5" />Wun dong wubedo ki jami lonyo mamalo tutwal ki yomcwiny i lobo; wupite ki cam, kun wucwe giwu, ento nino me ngolo ngutwu dong oromo! <verse eid="JAS 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 5:6" />Dong wutyeko ngolo kop me to ikom dano ma kitgi atir, gin bene gire gipeke ki lageng mo.<verse eid="JAS 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Diyo cwiny ki lega</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 5:7" />Kitmeno utmegina, wudii cwinywu nio wang ma Rwot bidwogo. Wunen kong kit ma lapur kuru kwede gin ma pire tek ma cek i lobo; en diyo cwinye nio wang ma kot me cwir ki me oro ocwer. <verse eid="JAS 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 5:8" />Wun bene wudii cwinywu, wucung matek, pien dwogo pa Rwot dong cok. <verse eid="JAS 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 5:9" />Pe wubed ki nguru, utmegina, ngat acel acel pe obed ki nguru ikom lawote, wek pe kingol kop ikomwu. Nen, Langolkop dong tye ocung i dogola. <verse eid="JAS 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 5:10" />Utmegina, lanen me ciro can ki diyo cwiny nen ikom lunebi mayam guloko inying Rwot. <verse eid="JAS 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 5:11" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5:11: a </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="JOB 1:21">Yub 1:21</ref>,<ref loc="JOB 1:22">22</ref>; <ref loc="JOB 2:10">2:10</ref>; </char><char style="xo" closed="false">b </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="PSA 103:8">Jab 103:8</ref></char></note> Jo mayam guciro can matek, walwongogi ni lugumkom. Wutyeko winyo bene kit macalo Yubu yam ociro kwede can, dok wuneno agiki me tic pa Rwot ikome, kit ma Rwot won kica timo kwede ber bot dano.<verse eid="JAS 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 5:12" />
    <note caller="-" style="x">
      <char style="xo" closed="false">5:12: </char>
      <char style="xt" closed="false">
        <ref loc="MAT 5:34-37">Mat 5:34-37</ref>
      </char>
    </note> Makatone ducu, utmegina, pe wukwong kwong ki nying polo, kadi ki nying lobo, kadi kit kwong mukene ducu; ento ye lokwu ducu myero obed ni, “Eyo,” nyo ni, “Pe,” wek pe kingol kop ikomwu.<verse eid="JAS 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 5:13" />Tye ngat mo ikinwu matye ki can? Myero oleg Lubanga. Tye ngat mo matye ki yomcwiny? Myero en ower wer me pako Lubanga. <verse eid="JAS 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 5:14" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5:14: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="MRK 6:13">Mar 6:13</ref></char></note> Tye ngat mo ikinwu ma kome lit? Myero en olwong ludongo me lwak pa Lubanga, wek guleg Lubanga pire kun giwire ki moo inying Rwot. <verse eid="JAS 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 5:15" />Lega ma niye tye iye bicango latwo, Rwot biile malo; kace onongo yam otimo bal mo, ci kibitime iye kica. <verse eid="JAS 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 5:16" />Pimeno, wutuc balwu, ngat acel acel otuc mere bot lawote, dok bene ngat acel acel myero oleg Lubanga pi lawote, wek wucang. Lega pa dano ma kite atir tek, tye ki twero madwong. <verse eid="JAS 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 5:17" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5:17: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="LUK 17:1">Luk 17:1</ref>; <ref loc="LUK 18:1">18:1</ref></char></note> Eliya yam obedo dano ma kite cal kwedwa, yam olego Lubanga matek ni kot pe ocwer, omiyo kot pe ocwer i lobo pi mwaka adek ki dwe abicel. <verse eid="JAS 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 5:18" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5:18: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="LUK 18:42-43">Luk 18:42-43</ref></char></note> Ka dok olego aye, omiyo kot ocako cwer, lobo oceko cam mabup.<verse eid="JAS 5:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 5:19" />Utmegina, kace dano mo ki ikinwu ongak woko ki i lok ada, ka ngat mukene aye dong odwoke cen, <verse eid="JAS 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 5:20" /><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">5:20: </char><char style="xt" closed="false"><ref loc="PRO 10:12">Car 10:12</ref>; <ref loc="1PE 4:8">1 Pet 4:8</ref></char></note> myero wunge ni, ka ngat ma okwanyo labalo ki i yone ma ogom odwoke cen, ngat meno bilaro kwone woko ki i to, dok biumu bale mapol.<verse eid="JAS 5:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 5" />
</usx>